Output Contents <code>*_tracked.mp4</code> boxes, temporary IDs, and trails; source audio is not copied <code>*_result.json</code> the serialized <code>VideoResults</code> — one record per frame with <code>frame_id</code>, <code>timestamp</code>, and tracked <code>instances</code> <code>*_tracks.csv</code> one row per active track per frame: time, ID, box, confidence and class <p>One JSON frame record has this shape:</p> <pre><code>{
  "frame_id": 42,
  "timestamp": 1.75,
  "instances": [
    {"box": [100.0, 120.0, 180.0, 220.0], "confidence": 0.94, "cls": 0, "id": 1}
  ]
}
</code></pre> <p>This is the same per-frame schema every <code>Video</code> pipeline produces (see the Video guide), so the output feeds any tooling that already consumes PhysioTrack results.</p> <p>A track ID is not identity recognition</p> <p>An ID is a temporary association inside one tracker run. It can change after a long occlusion, exit/re-entry, or association error. It is neither a name nor a biometric identity and must not be described as face recognition.</p>
